const STORIES = [
{id:'a1-lost-key',title:'The Lost Key',level:'A1',tone:'#F3C86A',emoji:'🔑',minutes:3,pages:[['🏠','Mia is at home. She cannot find her key.','ميا في المنزل. لا تستطيع العثور على مفتاحها.'],['🧥','She looks in her bag and under the chair. The key is not there.','تنظر في حقيبتها وتحت الكرسي. المفتاح ليس هناك.'],['🐶','Her little dog runs to the garden. Mia follows him and sees a shiny key near a flower.','يركض كلبها إلى الحديقة. تتبعه ميا وترى مفتاحًا لامعًا قرب زهرة.'],['😊','Mia picks up the key and opens the door. “Good dog!” she says.','تلتقط ميا المفتاح وتفتح الباب. تقول: كلب جيد!']],vocab:{key:['a small piece of metal used to open a lock','مفتاح','kee','I use my key to open the door.'],find:['to discover where something is','يعثر على','fynd','Can you find my bag?'],garden:['an area outside where plants grow','حديقة','GAR-dən','We play in the garden.'],shiny:['bright because light reflects from it','لامع','SHY-nee','The shiny coin is new.']},questions:[['Where does Mia find the key?',['In the garden','In her bag','Under the chair'],0,'The dog leads Mia to the garden, where she sees the key.'],['What does “shiny” mean here?',['Reflecting light','Very old','Very soft'],0,'The key reflects light, so it looks shiny.'],['Who helps Mia find the key?',['Her dog','Her sister','Her teacher'],0,'Mia follows her little dog to the garden.']]},
{id:'a1-rainy-picnic',title:'A Rainy Picnic',level:'A1',tone:'#91C9E8',emoji:'🧺',minutes:3,pages:[['🌳','Sam and his sister pack a picnic. They take apples, bread, and juice to the park.','يحضر سام وأخته نزهة ويأخذان التفاح والخبز والعصير إلى الحديقة.'],['☁️','They sit under a tree. Dark clouds cover the sky, and cold rain begins to fall.','يجلسان تحت شجرة. تغطي الغيوم الداكنة السماء ويبدأ المطر بالهطول.'],['🏃','Sam puts the food in the bag. They run to a small café near the park.','يضع سام الطعام في الحقيبة ويركضان إلى مقهى صغير قرب الحديقة.'],['☕','The café is warm and dry. They share their picnic and laugh about the rain.','المقهى دافئ وجاف. يتقاسمان طعام النزهة ويضحكان على المطر.']],vocab:{pack:['to put things into a bag for a trip','يحزم','pak','Pack your books before school.'],cloud:['a white or grey shape in the sky','سحابة','klowd','A dark cloud is over the house.'],share:['to use or enjoy something together','يتقاسم','shair','We share our lunch.'],dry:['not wet','جاف','dry','My coat is dry now.']},questions:[['Why do they leave the tree?',['It starts to rain','They are hungry','It is too hot'],0,'Cold rain begins to fall, so they move to the café.'],['What does “dry” mean?',['Not wet','Very cold','Full of food'],0,'They are safe from the rain inside the café.'],['What do they do in the café?',['Share their food','Buy a tree','Go swimming'],0,'They eat the picnic together and laugh.']]},
{id:'a2-night-train',title:'The Night Train',level:'A2',tone:'#A99BEA',emoji:'🚆',minutes:4,pages:[['🚉','Nora arrived at the station just before sunset. Her train was delayed, so she bought a warm drink.','وصلت نورا إلى المحطة قبل الغروب. تأخر قطارها فاشترت مشروبًا دافئًا.'],['🧳','While she was waiting, an older man asked whether she had seen a blue suitcase. He had left it near the ticket desk.','بينما كانت تنتظر، سألها رجل إن كانت قد رأت حقيبة زرقاء تركها قرب مكتب التذاكر.'],['🔎','Nora remembered seeing the suitcase beside a bench. They hurried back and found it exactly where he had described.','تذكرت نورا الحقيبة بجانب مقعد. عادا بسرعة ووجداها في المكان الذي وصفه.'],['🌙','When the train finally arrived, the man thanked Nora. She boarded feeling glad that a small detail had helped someone.','عندما وصل القطار، شكر الرجل نورا. صعدت سعيدة لأن تفصيلًا صغيرًا ساعد شخصًا.']],vocab:{delayed:['happening later than planned','متأخر','di-LAYD','Our flight was delayed.'],bench:['a long seat for several people','مقعد طويل','bench','We sat on a bench in the park.'],remember:['to bring something back into your mind','يتذكر','ri-MEM-ber','I remember your name.'],boarded:['got onto a train, bus, or plane','صعد إلى وسيلة نقل','BOR-did','They boarded the train at noon.']},questions:[['Why did Nora go back with the man?',['To look for his suitcase','To buy a ticket','To find a café'],0,'The man had left his blue suitcase near the station desk.'],['What does “delayed” mean?',['Later than expected','Very crowded','Already gone'],0,'Nora had to wait because the train did not arrive on time.'],['How did Nora feel at the end?',['Glad she had helped','Angry','Afraid'],0,'She felt good because remembering a detail helped someone.']]},
{id:'a2-bread-mystery',title:'The Missing Bread',level:'A2',tone:'#E8A27F',emoji:'🍞',minutes:4,pages:[['🥪','Every morning, Leo found one slice of bread missing from the kitchen. He blamed his brother, who always denied taking it.','كل صباح، كان ليو يجد شريحة خبز مفقودة. اتهم أخاه الذي كان ينكر أخذها.'],['🕵️','On Saturday, Leo woke up early and hid behind the door. He waited quietly with a notebook in his hand.','يوم السبت، استيقظ ليو مبكرًا واختبأ خلف الباب منتظرًا بهدوء.'],['🐈','At six, the cat jumped onto the counter and pulled the bread toward the floor. Leo had blamed the wrong person all week.','في السادسة، قفز القط إلى المنضدة وسحب الخبز. كان ليو يتهم الشخص الخطأ طوال الأسبوع.'],['😹','Leo apologised to his brother. The next day, they put the bread in a closed box and gave the cat a toy instead.','اعتذر ليو لأخيه. في اليوم التالي، وضعا الخبز في صندوق مغلق وأعطيا القط لعبة.']],vocab:{missing:['not present where expected','مفقود','MIS-ing','One page is missing from my book.'],blamed:['said someone was responsible for a problem','لامَ','blaymd','She blamed me for the mess.'],quietly:['without making much noise','بهدوء','KWY-it-lee','Please walk quietly.'],apologised:['said you were sorry','اعتذر','uh-POL-uh-jyzd','He apologised for being late.']},questions:[['Who took the bread?',['The cat','Leo’s brother','A neighbour'],0,'Leo sees the cat pull the bread from the counter.'],['What does “blamed” mean?',['Said someone caused the problem','Gave a gift','Asked a question'],0,'Leo said his brother was responsible, but he was wrong.'],['What did Leo do after?',['Apologised to his brother','Bought more cats','Hid the notebook'],0,'He said sorry because he had accused his brother unfairly.']]},
{id:'b1-last-bus',title:'The Last Bus',level:'B1',tone:'#75C7B0',emoji:'🚌',minutes:5,followUp:{taskId:'world-a2-on',label:'Practise the bridge in the village'},pages:[['🌆','By the time Daniel reached the stop, the last bus had already left. He was about to call a taxi when a cyclist slowed down beside him.','عندما وصل دانيال إلى الموقف، كان آخر حافلة قد غادرت. كان على وشك طلب سيارة أجرة حين أبطأت راكبة دراجة بجانبه.'],['🚲','The cyclist recognised him from the neighbourhood. “If you take the road beside the river, you can catch the bus at the next stop,” she said.','تعرفت عليه راكبة الدراجة من الحي وأخبرته أنه يستطيع اللحاق بالحافلة عند الموقف التالي.'],['🌉','Although he was tired, Daniel followed her advice. He reached the next stop just as the bus was turning the corner.','رغم تعبه، اتبع دانيال نصيحتها. وصل إلى الموقف بينما كانت الحافلة تنعطف.'],['🙌','He made it with seconds to spare. The next morning, he thanked the cyclist and decided to leave home earlier from then on.','لحق بالحافلة قبل فوات الأوان بثوانٍ. في الصباح شكر راكبة الدراجة وقرر الخروج أبكر.']],vocab:{recognised:['knew who someone was from before','تعرّف على','REK-ug-nyzd','I recognised her voice.'],advice:['a suggestion about what someone should do','نصيحة','ad-VYSS','My teacher gave me useful advice.'],although:['despite the fact that','رغم أن','awl-THOH','Although it was late, we continued.'],spare:['extra time remaining','وقت إضافي','spair','We arrived with five minutes to spare.']},questions:[['Why did Daniel change his route?',['A cyclist suggested a faster way','The road was closed','He wanted a walk'],0,'The cyclist told him how to reach another stop in time.'],['What does “with seconds to spare” mean?',['Just before it was too late','After hours','Without a watch'],0,'Daniel arrived only moments before the bus turned away.'],['What did Daniel decide?',['Leave home earlier','Buy a bicycle','Move away'],0,'He wanted to avoid missing the bus again.']]},
{id:'b1-quiet-lab',title:'The Quiet Lab',level:'B1',tone:'#8CB5E8',emoji:'🧪',minutes:5,pages:[['🔬','The school science lab had been quiet for weeks because its old sensor kept giving strange readings. Everyone assumed the equipment was broken.','ظل مختبر العلوم هادئًا لأسابيع لأن المستشعر القديم أعطى قراءات غريبة. افترض الجميع أن المعدات معطلة.'],['📒','When Amina checked the notes, she noticed that the readings changed whenever the window was open. She suggested testing the sensor in a closed room.','لاحظت أمينة أن القراءات تتغير كلما كانت النافذة مفتوحة، فاقترحت اختبار المستشعر في غرفة مغلقة.'],['🌡️','The next test confirmed her idea: a cold draft was affecting the instrument. After they sealed the window, the measurements became stable.','أكد الاختبار فكرتها: تيار هواء بارد كان يؤثر في الجهاز. بعد إغلاق النافذة، استقرت القياسات.'],['💡','The teacher praised Amina for looking for evidence instead of replacing the sensor. The lab soon became the busiest room in school.','أثنى المعلم على أمينة لأنها بحثت عن دليل بدل استبدال المستشعر. أصبح المختبر أكثر غرف المدرسة نشاطًا.']],vocab:{sensor:['a device that detects or measures something','مستشعر','SEN-sər','The sensor measures the temperature.'],assumed:['believed something without checking','افترض','uh-SOOMD','I assumed the shop was open.'],draft:['a current of air in a room','تيار هواء','draft','A cold draft came through the window.'],evidence:['facts that help show what is true','دليل','EV-i-dens','We need evidence before deciding.']},questions:[['What caused the strange readings?',['A cold draft from the window','A broken computer','A missing notebook'],0,'The sensor was affected by cold air entering through the open window.'],['What does “assumed” mean?',['Believed without checking','Measured carefully','Explained to a group'],0,'Everyone thought the equipment was broken before testing the idea.'],['Why did the teacher praise Amina?',['She looked for evidence','She bought equipment','She finished first'],0,'Amina investigated the cause instead of replacing the sensor immediately.']]},
{id:'b2-open-door',title:'The Open Door',level:'B2',tone:'#C49BE8',emoji:'🚪',minutes:6,pages:[['🏢','The new manager inherited a team that rarely spoke up. Meetings were polished but unproductive, and promising ideas were routinely swept under the rug.','ورث المدير فريقًا نادرًا ما يتحدث بصراحة. كانت الاجتماعات مرتبة لكنها غير منتجة، وكانت الأفكار الواعدة تُخفى باستمرار.'],['🗣️','Rather than imposing more rules, she invited everyone to share one concern anonymously. At first, the feedback was blunt; nevertheless, she listened without becoming defensive.','بدل فرض قواعد أخرى، دعت الجميع إلى مشاركة مشكلة دون أسماء. كان النقد صريحًا، ومع ذلك استمعت دون دفاعية.'],['🧩','Several comments pointed to the same bottleneck: every small decision required her approval. She had tried to keep things on track, but the process was holding the team back.','أشارت التعليقات إلى العائق نفسه: كل قرار صغير يحتاج موافقتها. كانت تحاول إبقاء الأمور منظمة لكن العملية أعاقت الفريق.'],['🌱','She delegated routine choices and kept the door open for difficult conversations. Within a month, the team took ownership and its hidden ideas began to flourish.','فوّضت القرارات الروتينية وأبقت الباب مفتوحًا للمحادثات الصعبة. خلال شهر، تحمل الفريق المسؤولية وبدأت أفكاره المخفية تزدهر.']],vocab:{'speak up':['to express an opinion openly','يتحدث بصراحة','speek up','Please speak up if you disagree.'],'swept':['hidden instead of being dealt with','أُخفي بدل معالجة المشكلة','swept','The mistake was swept under the rug.'],bottleneck:['a point that slows progress','عائق يبطئ التقدم','BOT-ul-nek','Approval became a bottleneck.'],delegated:['gave a task or decision to another person','فوّض','DEL-uh-gay-tid','She delegated some tasks.'],ownership:['acceptance of responsibility','تحمّل المسؤولية','OH-ner-ship','The team took ownership of the project.']},questions:[['Why were the meetings unproductive?',['People hid concerns and ideas','They were too short','The manager cancelled them'],0,'People rarely spoke up, so useful ideas stayed hidden.'],['What does “swept under the rug” mean?',['Hidden rather than addressed','Cleaned carefully','Shared with everyone'],0,'Problems were not openly discussed.'],['What changed after delegation?',['The team took more responsibility','All meetings stopped','The team became smaller'],0,'Giving people authority helped them take ownership.']]},
{id:'b2-second-chance',title:'A Second Chance',level:'B2',tone:'#E99BAF',emoji:'🎭',minutes:6,pages:[['🎤','Rafi had spent months preparing for a public speaking contest, yet he froze halfway through his opening. He was convinced he had blown his only chance.','استعد رافي أشهرًا لمسابقة الخطابة، لكنه تجمد في منتصف مقدمته. اقتنع أنه أضاع فرصته الوحيدة.'],['📝','His coach refused to sugar-coat the result, but reminded him that one bad performance did not define his ability. They reviewed the recording together.','رفضت مدربته تجميل النتيجة، لكنها ذكّرته بأن أداءً سيئًا واحدًا لا يحدد قدرته. راجعا التسجيل معًا.'],['🪞','Over the next few weeks, Rafi practised in front of friends and learned to pause when he lost his place. Gradually, he stopped treating every mistake as a disaster.','خلال الأسابيع التالية، تدرب رافي أمام أصدقائه وتعلم التوقف حين يفقد تسلسل كلامه. تدريجيًا توقف عن اعتبار كل خطأ كارثة.'],['🏆','At the next event, he delivered a calmer speech. He did not win, but listeners approached him afterward, and he turned a setback into useful experience.','في الفعالية التالية، ألقى خطابًا أهدأ. لم يفز، لكن مستمعين اقتربوا منه، وحوّل العثرة إلى خبرة مفيدة.']],vocab:{froze:['became unable to move or speak from fear','تجمّد من الخوف','frohz','I froze when everyone looked at me.'],'blown':['lost an opportunity through a mistake','أضاع فرصة','blohn','He thought he had blown his chance.'],'sugar-coat':['make something unpleasant sound better than it is','يجمّل الحقيقة','SHUG-er koht','I will not sugar-coat the feedback.'],setback:['a problem that delays progress','عثرة أو انتكاسة','SET-bak','A setback can teach you something.']},questions:[['Why did Rafi think he had failed?',['He froze during his speech','He forgot to attend','He lost his notes'],0,'He became unable to continue smoothly during the opening.'],['What does “sugar-coat” mean?',['Make bad news sound less bad','Prepare a dessert','Repeat a speech'],0,'The coach was honest instead of making the result sound better.'],['What did Rafi learn?',['Mistakes can become useful experience','He should never speak again','Winning is the only goal'],0,'He improved and gained confidence even without winning.']]}
,{id:'c1-quiet-objection',title:'The Quiet Objection',level:'C1',tone:'#A9B7E8',emoji:'🗣️',minutes:6,pages:[['🏢','Leila reviews a project schedule that assumes every supplier will deliver on time. The launch date looks realistic only if that assumption holds.','تراجع ليلى جدول مشروع يفترض أن جميع الموردين سيسلّمون في الموعد. يبدو موعد الإطلاق واقعيًا فقط إذا صحّ هذا الافتراض.'],['📝','Instead of rejecting the plan outright, she asks which delivery estimates are supported by evidence and which are still uncertain. The room falls quiet.','بدل رفض الخطة مباشرة، تسأل عن مواعيد التسليم المدعومة بالأدلة وتلك التي ما زالت غير مؤكدة. يعمّ الصمت الغرفة.'],['🔍','The team checks recent supplier records and discovers that one critical component often arrives late. Leila suggests comparing the cost of a small delay with the cost of keeping a backup supplier.','يراجع الفريق سجلات الموردين الحديثة ويكتشف أن أحد المكوّنات الأساسية يتأخر كثيرًا. تقترح ليلى مقارنة تكلفة التأخير القصير بتكلفة تجهيز مورد بديل.'],['🤝','The team adds a contingency and adjusts the schedule before the problem occurs. Leila’s measured objection protects the launch date—and shows that challenging an assumption can strengthen a plan.','يضيف الفريق خطة احتياطية ويعدّل الجدول قبل وقوع المشكلة. يحمي اعتراض ليلى المتزن موعد الإطلاق، ويُظهر أن مراجعة الافتراضات قد تجعل الخطة أقوى.']],decision:{afterPage:1,prompt:'The team is uncomfortable with Leila’s question. What should she do next?',options:[{text:'Ask for the evidence behind the estimates and invite the team to review it together.',response:'This keeps the discussion focused on evidence, gives colleagues a shared problem to solve, and avoids turning the question into a personal confrontation.'},{text:'Withdraw the concern so the meeting can finish on time.',response:'This may preserve short-term comfort, but the uncertainty remains hidden and the team loses a chance to reduce the risk.'},{text:'Insist that the schedule is wrong before checking the records.',response:'Raising a risk matters, but declaring the plan wrong before checking evidence can weaken trust and make a useful concern easier to dismiss.'}]},vocab:{assumption:['something accepted as true without complete proof','افتراض','uh-SUMP-shun','The plan rests on an assumption.'],contingency:['a plan for a possible problem','خطة احتياطية','kun-TIN-juhn-see','We prepared a contingency.'],measured:['calm and carefully considered','متزن ومدروس','MEZH-erd','She gave a measured response.'],outright:['completely or immediately, without hesitation','بشكل قاطع','OWT-ryte','He did not reject the idea outright.'],estimate:['a careful guess about an amount, cost, or time','تقدير','ES-ti-mit','The delivery estimate was too optimistic.'],critical:['extremely important to success','أساسي / بالغ الأهمية','KRIT-i-kəl','The critical component arrived late.'],withdraw:['to take back or remove something','يتراجع عن / يسحب','with-DRAW','She decided not to withdraw her concern.']},questions:[['Why does Leila question the schedule?',['It relies on untested assumptions','She dislikes the supplier','She wants to cancel the project'],0,'The schedule depends on every supplier delivering on time, but this has not been verified.'],['What is a contingency in this context?',['A backup plan for a possible problem','A final invoice','A meeting summary'],0,'A contingency prepares the team for a risk, such as a late delivery.'],['What is the strongest lesson from the story?',['Evidence-based objections can improve a plan','Disagreement always harms teams','A plan should never change'],0,'Leila checks the evidence, raises the risk constructively, and helps the team prepare before the problem occurs.']]}
,{id:'c1-cost-of-clarity',title:'The Cost of Clarity',level:'C1',tone:'#8BCFC2',emoji:'🔎',minutes:5,pages:[['📊','A report says a process is faster but omits extra maintenance hours.','يقول تقرير إن العملية أسرع لكنه يغفل ساعات الصيانة الإضافية.'],['🧾','Omar asks the authors to disclose hidden costs and limits.','يطلب عمر توضيح التكاليف الخفية والحدود.'],['💡','The revised report is more useful for decision-makers.','يصبح التقرير المعدّل أنفع لصناع القرار.']],vocab:{omit:['to leave something out','يغفل','oh-MIT','The summary omitted a cost.'],tradeoff:['a balance between competing things','مفاضلة','TRAYD-off','Speed involves a trade-off.'],qualify:['to limit a claim carefully','يقيّد ادعاءً','KWOL-uh-fy','The evidence qualifies the claim.']},questions:[['What does the report omit?',['Maintenance costs','The title','The date'],0,'It leaves out maintenance hours.'],['Why is the revised report better?',['It explains limits and trade-offs','It sounds dramatic','It removes uncertainty'],0,'Readers can make an informed decision.'],['What does qualify a claim mean?',['Explain its limits','Repeat it','Delete evidence'],0,'It clarifies when a claim is valid.']]}
,{id:'c2-language-of-consensus',title:'The Language of Consensus',level:'C2',tone:'#C6A7E8',emoji:'⚖️',minutes:6,pages:[['🏛️','A committee appears unanimous, but some members stay silent under pressure.','تبدو اللجنة مجمعة، لكن بعض الأعضاء يصمتون تحت الضغط.'],['🧩','Mariam distinguishes genuine agreement from acquiescence and invites objections.','تميّز مريم بين الاتفاق الحقيقي والإذعان وتدعو إلى الاعتراضات.'],['🌱','The final decision gains support because dissent was examined.','يحظى القرار بدعم لأن الآراء المخالفة نوقشت.']],vocab:{unanimous:['in agreement by everyone','بالإجماع','yoo-NAN-uh-mus','The vote was unanimous.'],acquiescence:['acceptance without protest','إذعان','ak-wee-ESS-ens','Silence is not always acquiescence.'],dissent:['a different opinion expressed openly','رأي مخالف','dih-SENT','The chair welcomed dissent.']},questions:[['Why may agreement be misleading?',['Some members feel pressured to stay silent','Everyone changed votes','The proposal vanished'],0,'The chair discourages objections.'],['What distinction does Mariam make?',['Agreement versus reluctant acceptance','Speed versus accuracy','Writing versus speaking'],0,'She separates consensus from acquiescence.'],['Why does the decision gain support?',['Opposing arguments were examined','Disagreement was banned','The meeting ended early'],0,'Examining dissent strengthens decisions.']]}
,{id:'c2-unintended-inference',title:'The Unintended Inference',level:'C2',tone:'#E9A9B6',emoji:'🧠',minutes:6,pages:[['📩','A director calls a proposal “ambitious.” Some hear praise; others infer it is unrealistic.','يصف مدير مقترحًا بأنه طموح؛ فيراه البعض مدحًا وآخرون يرونه غير واقعي.'],['💬','Nabil asks what evidence would distinguish encouragement from polite scepticism.','يسأل نبيل عن الأدلة التي تميّز التشجيع من التشكيك المهذب.'],['🧭','The director clarifies that the goal is worthwhile but milestones need justification.','يوضح المدير أن الهدف مهم لكن المراحل تحتاج إلى تبرير.']],vocab:{infer:['to reach a conclusion from clues','يستنتج','in-FUR','Readers may infer criticism.'],self_evident:['seeming obvious without explanation','بديهي','self-EV-i-dent','The answer was not self-evident.'],milestone:['an important stage in a process','مرحلة رئيسية','MYL-stohn','Each milestone needs an owner.']},questions:[['Why is “ambitious” interpreted differently?',['Its implication depends on context','No adjective was used','The proposal was hidden'],0,'The word can imply praise or doubt.'],['What does Nabil ask for?',['Evidence to clarify meaning','A new director','A shorter report'],0,'He asks how interpretations can be distinguished.'],['What changes at the end?',['Vague wording becomes specific feedback','The project is cancelled','Milestones are ignored'],0,'The director explains what needs work.']]},
{"id":"a1-blue-umbrella","title":"The Blue Umbrella","level":"A1","tone":"#82BDE8","emoji":"☂️","minutes":3,"pages":[["🌦️","It is raining. Ana has a blue umbrella.","إنها تمطر. لدى آنا مظلة زرقاء."],["🚌","At the bus stop, she sees an old man without an umbrella.","في موقف الحافلة، ترى رجلًا مسنًا بلا مظلة."],["🙂","Ana shares her umbrella with him. They get on the bus together.","تشاركه آنا مظلتها. يصعدان إلى الحافلة معًا."]],"vocab":{"umbrella":["a cover that keeps rain off you","مظلة","um-BREL-uh","Take an umbrella when it rains."],"share":["to use or give something together","يشارك","shair","I share my book with my friend."],"rain":["water that falls from clouds","مطر","rayn","The rain is cold."],"together":["with another person or group","معًا","tuh-GETH-er","We walk together."]},"questions":[["What is the weather like?",["Rainy","Very hot","Snowy"],0,"The first page says it is raining."],["Who has no umbrella?",["An old man","Ana's teacher","The bus driver"],0,"Ana sees an old man without an umbrella."],["What does Ana do?",["She shares her umbrella","She goes home","She buys a bus"],0,"Ana helps the man by sharing her umbrella."]]},
{"id":"a1-helpful-neighbor","title":"A Helpful Neighbor","level":"A1","tone":"#8CC7A1","emoji":"🪴","minutes":3,"pages":[["🏡","Ben has a small garden. He waters the flowers every morning.","لدى بن حديقة صغيرة. يسقي الأزهار كل صباح."],["🪣","One day, his water bucket breaks. The flowers are dry.","في أحد الأيام، ينكسر دلو الماء. تصبح الأزهار جافة."],["🌷","His neighbor gives him a new bucket. Ben waters the flowers and says thank you.","تعطيه جارته دلوًا جديدًا. يسقي بن الأزهار ويشكرها."]],"vocab":{"neighbor":["a person who lives near you","جار","NAY-ber","My neighbor lives next door."],"bucket":["a container for carrying water","دلو","BUK-it","The bucket is full of water."],"water":["the clear liquid people drink and use for plants","ماء","WAW-ter","Plants need water."],"broken":["damaged and not working","مكسور","BROH-ken","The old cup is broken."]},"questions":[["What does Ben do every morning?",["Waters the flowers","Paints the house","Cooks soup"],0,"Ben waters his garden each morning."],["Why are the flowers dry?",["His bucket breaks","It is winter","He sells them"],0,"The broken bucket makes watering difficult."],["How does the neighbor help?",["She gives him a bucket","She cuts the flowers","She takes his garden"],0,"She gives Ben a new bucket."]]},
{"id":"a1-wrong-lunchbox","title":"The Wrong Lunchbox","level":"A1","tone":"#E8B77E","emoji":"🍱","minutes":3,"pages":[["🏫","Lina takes a yellow lunchbox to school. It has a sandwich and an apple.","تأخذ لينا علبة طعام صفراء إلى المدرسة. فيها شطيرة وتفاحة."],["🍎","At lunch, she opens it and finds a note. The food is not hers.","وقت الغداء، تفتحها وتجد ورقة. الطعام ليس لها."],["🤝","Lina checks the name. She gives the lunchbox to Omar and finds her own.","تتحقق لينا من الاسم. تعطي علبة الطعام لعمر وتجد علبتها."]],"vocab":{"lunchbox":["a box used to carry food","علبة طعام","LUNCH-boks","My lunchbox is in my bag."],"sandwich":["food made with filling between bread","شطيرة","SAND-wich","I eat a cheese sandwich."],"note":["a short piece of writing","ملاحظة","noht","There is a note on the table."],"own":["belonging to you","خاص بك","ohn","This is my own bag."]},"questions":[["What color is Lina's lunchbox?",["Yellow","Blue","Green"],0,"Lina takes a yellow lunchbox to school."],["What does Lina find inside?",["A note","A toy car","A key"],0,"She opens the box and finds a note."],["How does Lina solve the problem?",["She checks the name","She throws the food away","She hides the box"],0,"She checks the name and returns Omar's lunchbox."]]},
{"id":"a1-note-grandma","title":"A Note for Grandma","level":"A1","tone":"#E8A9C3","emoji":"💌","minutes":3,"pages":[["✏️","Tom wants to visit Grandma. He writes a short note for her.","يريد توم زيارة جدته. يكتب لها رسالة قصيرة."],["🚲","He puts the note in his bag and rides his bike to her house.","يضع الرسالة في حقيبته ويركب دراجته إلى منزلها."],["❤️","Grandma reads the note and smiles. They make tea and talk.","تقرأ الجدة الرسالة وتبتسم. يحضّران الشاي ويتحدثان."]],"vocab":{"visit":["to go and see a person or place","يزور","VIZ-it","We visit Grandma on Sunday."],"write":["to make words with a pen or keyboard","يكتب","ryt","I write a short note."],"smile":["to make a happy expression","يبتسم","smyl","She smiles at her friend."],"tea":["a hot drink made with leaves","شاي","tee","Grandma makes tea."]},"questions":[["Who does Tom want to visit?",["His grandma","His coach","His neighbor"],0,"Tom wants to visit Grandma."],["Where does he put the note?",["In his bag","Under a tree","On the bus"],0,"He puts the note in his bag."],["How does Grandma feel when she reads it?",["Happy","Angry","Sleepy"],0,"Grandma smiles after reading the note."]]},
{"id":"a2-library-card","title":"The Library Card","level":"A2","tone":"#8BB6E8","emoji":"📚","minutes":3,"pages":[["📖","Nora wants to borrow a mystery book, but she has never used the town library.","تريد نورا استعارة كتاب غموض، لكنها لم تستخدم مكتبة المدينة من قبل."],["🪪","The librarian explains that she needs a library card and a form with her address.","تشرح أمينة المكتبة أنها تحتاج إلى بطاقة مكتبة واستمارة تتضمن عنوانها."],["✨","Nora fills in the form, receives her card, and borrows the book for two weeks.","تملأ نورا الاستمارة وتحصل على بطاقتها وتستعير الكتاب لمدة أسبوعين."]],"vocab":{"borrow":["to take something for a time and return it later","يستعير","BOR-oh","You can borrow books from a library."],"librarian":["a person who works in a library","أمين مكتبة","ly-BRAIR-ee-un","The librarian helped me find a book."],"form":["a document you fill in with information","استمارة","form","Please complete this form."],"address":["the details of where someone lives","عنوان","uh-DRES","Write your address here."]},"questions":[["What does Nora want to borrow?",["A mystery book","A bicycle","A cooking pot"],0,"Nora wants to borrow a mystery book."],["What does she need before borrowing?",["A library card and a form","A train ticket","A school uniform"],0,"The librarian explains the card and form requirements."],["How long can Nora keep the book?",["Two weeks","One day","One year"],0,"The story says she borrows it for two weeks."]]},
{"id":"a2-room-for-two","title":"A Room for Two","level":"A2","tone":"#C3A7E8","emoji":"🛏️","minutes":3,"pages":[["🧳","Maya and her cousin arrive at a small hotel after a long journey. They booked one room.","تصل مايا وابن عمها إلى فندق صغير بعد رحلة طويلة. لقد حجزا غرفة واحدة."],["🔑","At reception, the clerk finds their booking but notices that the room has only one bed.","في الاستقبال، يجد الموظف الحجز لكنه يلاحظ أن الغرفة فيها سرير واحد فقط."],["🛎️","Maya explains their needs politely. The clerk checks another room and gives them a room with two beds.","تشرح مايا احتياجاتهما بأدب. يفحص الموظف غرفة أخرى ويمنحهما غرفة بسريرين."]],"vocab":{"booking":["an arrangement made in advance","حجز","BOOK-ing","Our booking is for Friday."],"reception":["the desk where guests arrive at a hotel","الاستقبال","ri-SEP-shun","Ask at reception for your key."],"clerk":["a person who works at a desk or counter","موظف","klurk","The clerk checked our booking."],"politely":["in a respectful way","بأدب","puh-LYTE-lee","She asked politely for help."]},"questions":[["What is wrong with the first room?",["It has only one bed","It has no window","It is in another town"],0,"The clerk notices the room has one bed."],["What does Maya do?",["Explains their needs politely","Cancels every hotel","Leaves without speaking"],0,"Maya explains the problem calmly."],["What is the final solution?",["They get a room with two beds","They sleep outside","They buy a bed"],0,"The clerk finds a suitable room."]]},
{"id":"a2-early-delivery","title":"The Early Delivery","level":"A2","tone":"#D6B17A","emoji":"📦","minutes":3,"pages":[["📦","A package for Karim arrives two days earlier than expected. He is at work when the delivery driver calls.","تصل طردة كريم قبل الموعد المتوقع بيومين. يكون في العمل عندما يتصل سائق التوصيل."],["📱","Karim checks the tracking message and asks whether the driver can leave the package with the building manager.","يتحقق كريم من رسالة التتبع ويسأل إن كان السائق يستطيع ترك الطرد لدى مسؤول المبنى."],["🏢","The driver agrees after Karim confirms the manager’s name. Karim collects the package safely that evening.","يوافق السائق بعدما يؤكد كريم اسم المسؤول. يستلم كريم الطرد بأمان في المساء."]],"vocab":{"package":["a parcel sent to someone","طرد","PAK-ij","The package arrived today."],"expected":["thought likely to happen","متوقّع","ik-SPEK-tid","The delivery was expected on Friday."],"tracking":["information showing where a parcel is","تتبّع","TRAK-ing","Use the tracking number online."],"confirm":["to check that something is correct","يؤكد","kun-FURM","Please confirm the address."]},"questions":[["Why can Karim not receive the package himself?",["He is at work","He is on a plane","He lost his phone"],0,"The driver calls while Karim is at work."],["What does Karim check?",["The tracking message","A restaurant menu","A weather map"],0,"He checks the delivery tracking message."],["Why does he confirm the manager's name?",["To make sure the package goes to the right person","To change the package color","To cancel the order"],0,"Confirming the name supports a safe handover."]]},
{"id":"a2-garden-map","title":"The Garden Map","level":"A2","tone":"#91C7A6","emoji":"🗺️","minutes":3,"pages":[["🌿","A school group visits a large public garden. Their guide gives each pair a map and a list of plants to find.","تزور مجموعة مدرسية حديقة عامة كبيرة. يعطي المرشد كل ثنائي خريطة وقائمة نباتات للعثور عليها."],["🗺️","Yasmin and Adam follow the path, but a sign points in two directions. They stop to compare the map with the sign.","تتبع ياسمين وآدم المسار، لكن لافتة تشير إلى اتجاهين. يتوقفان لمقارنة الخريطة باللافتة."],["🌻","They choose the marked eastern path and find the sunflower bed before the group meeting time.","يختاران المسار الشرقي المحدد ويصلان إلى أحواض دوار الشمس قبل موعد اجتماع المجموعة."]],"vocab":{"guide":["a person who shows visitors around","مرشد","gyd","The guide explained the garden rules."],"map":["a drawing that shows where places are","خريطة","map","The map shows the path."],"direction":["the way something points or moves","اتجاه","di-REK-shun","Which direction should we take?"],"path":["a way for people to walk","مسار","path","Follow the path to the gate."]},"questions":[["What does the guide give the students?",["A map and a plant list","A train ticket","A cooking lesson"],0,"Each pair receives a map and a list of plants."],["Why do Yasmin and Adam stop?",["The sign points in two directions","They lose their lunch","The garden closes"],0,"They stop to compare the confusing sign with the map."],["Which path do they choose?",["The marked eastern path","A path outside the garden","No path at all"],0,"They choose the marked eastern path."]]},
{"id":"b1-unsent-message","title":"The Unsent Message","level":"B1","tone":"#8CBED8","emoji":"📱","minutes":4,"pages":[["💬","After a tense team meeting, Daniel writes a message saying that his colleague ignored an important warning. He is ready to send it immediately.","بعد اجتماع متوتر، يكتب دانيال رسالة يقول فيها إن زميله تجاهل تحذيرًا مهمًا. وهو مستعد لإرسالها فورًا."],["⏸️","Before sending it, he rereads the message and realizes that he does not know whether his colleague saw the warning. He saves the draft instead.","قبل الإرسال، يعيد قراءة الرسالة ويدرك أنه لا يعرف إن كان زميله قد رأى التحذير. فيحفظ المسودة بدلًا من ذلك."],["🤝","The next morning, Daniel asks what happened. His colleague explains that the warning was buried in an old thread. They agree on a clearer alert system.","في الصباح التالي، يسأل دانيال عمّا حدث. يوضح زميله أن التحذير كان مدفونًا في محادثة قديمة. ويتفقان على نظام تنبيه أوضح."]],"vocab":{"tense":["making you feel nervous or strained","متوتر","tens","The meeting became tense."],"draft":["a version of a message not yet sent","مسودة","draft","I saved the draft before sending."],"assume":["to accept something as true without proof","يفترض","uh-SOOM","Do not assume you know what happened."],"buried":["hidden under or among other things","مدفون / مخفي","BAIR-eed","The alert was buried in a long email thread."]},"questions":[["Why does Daniel pause before sending the message?",["He realizes he lacks key information","He forgets his colleague's name","He wants to delete the project"],0,"He does not know whether his colleague saw the warning."],["Where was the warning?",["In an old message thread","On a printed poster","In a public announcement"],0,"The colleague explains that the warning was buried in an old thread."],["What do they agree to change?",["The alert system","The project goal","The office location"],0,"They agree to make alerts clearer."]]},
{"id":"b1-small-repair","title":"A Small Repair","level":"B1","tone":"#D3AA75","emoji":"🔧","minutes":4,"pages":[["🚲","Amina’s bicycle chain slips off on her way to class. She is late, but she decides not to force the pedals.","ينفلت جنزير دراجة أمينة في طريقها إلى الدرس. إنها متأخرة، لكنها تقرر ألا تضغط على الدواسات بالقوة."],["🔍","She moves to a safe place, turns the bicycle upside down, and checks how the chain sits on the gears. She remembers a repair video she watched.","تنتقل إلى مكان آمن، وتقلب الدراجة، وتفحص موضع الجنزير على التروس. وتتذكر فيديو إصلاح شاهدته."],["🚴","After carefully replacing the chain, she tests the brakes and rides slowly to a nearby workshop for a quick safety check.","بعد إعادة الجنزير بحذر، تختبر المكابح وتقود ببطء إلى ورشة قريبة لإجراء فحص سريع للسلامة."]],"vocab":{"chain":["a series of linked metal parts that moves a bicycle","جنزير","chayn","The bicycle chain came loose."],"force":["to use strength to make something move","قوة / يجبر","fors","Do not force a stuck part."],"gear":["a toothed wheel used in a machine","ترس","geer","The chain slipped off the gear."],"safety":["protection from danger or harm","سلامة","SAYF-tee","Check the brakes for safety."]},"questions":[["What does Amina avoid doing?",["Forcing the pedals","Moving to a safe place","Checking the chain"],0,"She decides not to force the pedals."],["Why does she check the gears?",["To understand how the chain fits","To clean her school bag","To find a bus ticket"],0,"She checks the chain's position on the gears."],["What does she do after repairing the chain?",["Tests the brakes and gets a safety check","Races down a hill","Throws away the bicycle"],0,"She tests the brakes and visits a workshop."]]},
{"id":"b1-shared-budget","title":"The Shared Budget","level":"B1","tone":"#A7C9A1","emoji":"🧾","minutes":4,"pages":[["💰","Four students plan a science display. They have a limited budget and each person suggests different materials.","يخطط أربعة طلاب لإعداد عرض علمي. ميزانيتهم محدودة ويقترح كل شخص مواد مختلفة."],["📋","Rather than voting immediately, Sara lists what the display must demonstrate and compares prices, quality, and reuse options.","بدل التصويت فورًا، تكتب سارة ما يجب أن يوضحه العرض وتقارن الأسعار والجودة وإمكانية إعادة الاستخدام."],["🧪","The group chooses sturdy reusable parts and borrows one tool from the laboratory. They finish the display without exceeding the budget.","تختار المجموعة أجزاء متينة قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام وتستعير أداة من المختبر. وتنهي العرض دون تجاوز الميزانية."]],"vocab":{"budget":["the amount of money available for a purpose","ميزانية","BUJ-it","We must stay within our budget."],"reuse":["to use something again","يعيد الاستخدام","ree-YOOZ","We can reuse the cardboard."],"sturdy":["strong and unlikely to break","متين","STUR-dee","The sturdy stand holds the model."],"exceed":["to go beyond a limit","يتجاوز","ik-SEED","The cost must not exceed the budget."]},"questions":[["Why does Sara make a list first?",["To identify what the display must do","To choose the most expensive item","To end the project"],0,"She defines the requirements before comparing materials."],["What factors does she compare?",["Price, quality, and reuse","Color only","The students' ages"],0,"The story lists price, quality, and reuse options."],["How does the group stay within budget?",["They reuse parts and borrow a tool","They buy every tool","They remove the science display"],0,"Reusable parts and a borrowed tool reduce costs."]]},
{"id":"b1-missing-minutes","title":"The Missing Minutes","level":"B1","tone":"#C7B2E8","emoji":"🗒️","minutes":4,"pages":[["🕒","After a club meeting, Yusuf writes a summary. Two members say that the agreed deadline is missing from his notes.","بعد اجتماع النادي، يكتب يوسف ملخصًا. يقول عضوان إن الموعد النهائي المتفق عليه غير موجود في ملاحظاته."],["📨","Yusuf checks the chat and finds two different dates. Instead of choosing one, he asks the group to confirm what was agreed.","يتحقق يوسف من المحادثة ويجد تاريخين مختلفين. وبدل اختيار أحدهما، يطلب من المجموعة تأكيد ما تم الاتفاق عليه."],["✅","The members discover that one date was a suggestion and the other was the final decision. Yusuf corrects the summary and labels future decisions clearly.","يكتشف الأعضاء أن أحد التاريخين كان اقتراحًا والآخر هو القرار النهائي. يصحح يوسف الملخص ويتفقون على تمييز القرارات المستقبلية بوضوح."]],"vocab":{"summary":["a short statement of the main points","ملخص","SUM-uh-ree","Send a summary after the meeting."],"deadline":["the latest time to finish something","موعد نهائي","DED-lyn","The deadline is next Monday."],"confirm":["to make sure something is correct","يؤكد","kun-FURM","Please confirm the final date."],"suggestion":["an idea offered for consideration","اقتراح","suh-JES-chun","That date was only a suggestion."]},"questions":[["What problem do the members notice?",["The deadline is missing","The room is too cold","The club has no name"],0,"They say the agreed deadline is missing from the notes."],["Why does Yusuf ask the group?",["Two different dates appear in the chat","He has lost the summary","He wants to cancel the meeting"],0,"The chat contains two dates, and he does not know which is final."],["What do they change for future meetings?",["They label decisions clearly","They stop writing summaries","They use fewer messages only"],0,"They agree to distinguish final decisions from suggestions."]]},
{"id":"b2-honest-estimate","title":"The Honest Estimate","level":"B2","tone":"#86C7C1","emoji":"📊","minutes":4,"pages":[["📈","A project manager asks Noor how long a software migration will take. The team has completed similar work, but this system contains unfamiliar components.","يسأل مدير المشروع نور عن المدة اللازمة لنقل نظام برمجي. أنجز الفريق أعمالًا مشابهة، لكن هذا النظام يحتوي على مكونات غير مألوفة."],["🧮","Noor gives a range rather than a single confident date. She explains which tasks are well understood and which depend on testing an old interface.","تعطي نور نطاقًا زمنيًا بدل تاريخ واحد واثق. وتشرح المهام المفهومة جيدًا وتلك التي تعتمد على اختبار واجهة قديمة."],["🤝","The team runs a short technical test, narrows the estimate, and agrees on a review point. The manager can now plan without mistaking uncertainty for failure.","يجري الفريق اختبارًا تقنيًا قصيرًا ويضيّق النطاق ويتفق على موعد للمراجعة. يستطيع المدير التخطيط دون اعتبار عدم اليقين فشلًا."]],"vocab":{"migration":["moving a system or process to a new environment","نقل نظام","my-GRAY-shun","The migration needs careful testing."],"component":["one part of a larger system","مكوّن","kum-POH-nent","This component is unfamiliar."],"range":["the space between a lower and upper value","نطاق","raynj","Give a range for the estimated time."],"uncertainty":["the state of not being fully sure","عدم يقين","un-SUR-tun-tee","The test reduces uncertainty."]},"questions":[["Why does Noor avoid giving one exact date?",["Some components are unfamiliar","The team has no experience at all","The manager did not ask"],0,"The unfamiliar components make a single confident date unreliable."],["What does the team test?",["An old interface","A new office","The manager's calendar"],0,"The estimate depends on testing an old interface."],["What is the benefit of the review point?",["The team can update the plan as evidence improves","It guarantees there will be no problems","It removes the need to communicate"],0,"A review point lets the team revise the estimate using new evidence."]]},
{"id":"b2-better-handoff","title":"A Better Handoff","level":"B2","tone":"#B4A6E4","emoji":"🔄","minutes":4,"pages":[["📂","A support team repeatedly receives incomplete reports when a shift ends. The next team spends time asking for details that should already be recorded.","يتلقى فريق الدعم تقارير ناقصة باستمرار عند انتهاء المناوبة. ويقضي الفريق التالي وقتًا في طلب تفاصيل كان ينبغي تسجيلها."],["🧩","Marek reviews several cases and notices the same gaps: current status, actions already tried, and the next owner. He proposes a short handoff template.","يراجع ماريك عدة حالات ويلاحظ الثغرات نفسها: الحالة الحالية، والإجراءات المجربة، والمسؤول التالي. يقترح نموذج تسليم مختصرًا."],["📋","After a week, the team compares response times and missing details. The template helps, but they simplify one field that staff rarely use.","بعد أسبوع، يقارن الفريق أوقات الاستجابة والتفاصيل الناقصة. يساعد النموذج، لكنهم يبسطون خانة نادرًا ما يستخدمها الموظفون."]],"vocab":{"handoff":["the transfer of responsibility or information","تسليم المسؤولية","HAND-off","A clear handoff prevents confusion."],"incomplete":["not having all the necessary parts","غير مكتمل","in-kum-PLEET","The report was incomplete."],"template":["a reusable pattern or form","نموذج","TEM-plit","Use the template for every case."],"simplify":["to make something easier to use or understand","يبسّط","SIM-pluh-fy","We should simplify the form."]},"questions":[["What problem does the team face?",["Reports lack important details","There are too many customers","The office is closing"],0,"The next team repeatedly receives incomplete reports."],["What does Marek propose?",["A short handoff template","A longer meeting every day","A new support department"],0,"He proposes a template with status, actions tried, and next owner."],["Why do they simplify a field?",["Staff rarely use it","It contains all the key information","The template is no longer needed"],0,"They review usage and simplify a field that is rarely used."]]},
{"id":"b2-quiet-customer","title":"The Quiet Customer","level":"B2","tone":"#E6B48A","emoji":"🛍️","minutes":4,"pages":[["🛒","A shop team celebrates positive reviews, yet one regular customer has stopped returning. The manager assumes the customer found a cheaper shop.","يحتفل فريق متجر بالتقييمات الإيجابية، لكن زبونًا دائمًا توقف عن العودة. يفترض المدير أن الزبون وجد متجرًا أرخص."],["👂","A staff member contacts the customer politely and asks about the experience. The customer says the new self-checkout is confusing and no one seems available to help.","يتواصل موظف مع الزبون بأدب ويسأله عن تجربته. يقول الزبون إن الدفع الذاتي الجديد مربك ولا يبدو أن أحدًا متاح للمساعدة."],["🧰","The shop adds clearer signs and schedules a staff member near the machines at busy times. The team tracks whether customers need less assistance over the next month.","يضيف المتجر لافتات أوضح ويخصص موظفًا قرب الأجهزة في أوقات الازدحام. ويتابع الفريق ما إذا كان العملاء يحتاجون مساعدة أقل خلال الشهر التالي."]],"vocab":{"regular":["happening often or on a repeated basis","منتظم / دائم","REG-yuh-ler","She is a regular customer."],"assume":["to believe something without checking","يفترض","uh-SOOM","Do not assume the reason."],"self-checkout":["a machine customers use to pay without a cashier","الدفع الذاتي","self-CHECK-out","The self-checkout was confusing."],"schedule":["to plan a time for an activity","يجدول","SKEJ-ool","They schedule staff for busy times."]},"questions":[["What does the manager first assume?",["The customer found a cheaper shop","The customer moved away","The shop is too far"],0,"The manager assumes price is the reason without checking."],["What problem does the customer describe?",["Confusing self-checkout and little help","High prices only","Poor product quality"],0,"The customer describes confusion and a lack of visible assistance."],["How will the team evaluate the changes?",["Track assistance needs over a month","Count only positive reviews","Remove all checkout machines"],0,"They plan to track whether customers need less help."]]},
{"id":"b2-data-gap","title":"The Data Gap","level":"B2","tone":"#89B7D9","emoji":"📉","minutes":4,"pages":[["📊","A school compares attendance before and after a new reminder system. The report shows fewer absences, so the team prepares to call the system a success.","تقارن مدرسة الحضور قبل نظام تذكير جديد وبعده. يُظهر التقرير انخفاض الغياب، فيستعد الفريق لاعتبار النظام ناجحًا."],["🔎","A teacher notices that the later data covers fewer school days because of a holiday. The comparison may therefore exaggerate the improvement.","تلاحظ معلمة أن البيانات اللاحقة تغطي أيامًا دراسية أقل بسبب عطلة. لذلك قد تبالغ المقارنة في تقدير التحسن."],["🧮","The team compares equivalent weeks and checks several classes separately. The improvement remains, but it is smaller than the first report suggested.","تقارن المجموعة أسابيع متكافئة وتفحص عدة صفوف كلًا على حدة. يظل التحسن موجودًا، لكنه أقل مما أوحى به التقرير الأول."]],"vocab":{"attendance":["the act of being present at a place","الحضور","uh-TEN-duns","Attendance improved this term."],"absence":["a time when someone is not present","غياب","AB-suns","The report counts each absence."],"equivalent":["equal in value, amount, or purpose","متكافئ","ih-KWIV-uh-lunt","Compare equivalent weeks."],"exaggerate":["to describe something as greater than it is","يبالغ","ig-ZAJ-uh-rayt","The first report may exaggerate the change."]},"questions":[["Why might the first report exaggerate improvement?",["The periods cover different numbers of school days","The school has no attendance data","The reminder system was never used"],0,"A holiday means the later period includes fewer school days."],["What does the team compare next?",["Equivalent weeks and separate classes","Only the first day","The price of textbooks"],0,"They compare equivalent periods and inspect classes separately."],["What is the final finding?",["Improvement remains but is smaller","Attendance becomes zero","The system is proven useless"],0,"The corrected comparison still shows improvement, but less than first reported."]]},
{"id":"c1-fragile-forecast","title":"The Fragile Forecast","level":"C1","tone":"#86BFC8","emoji":"🌦️","minutes":5,"pages":[["📈","A logistics team forecasts a sharp rise in demand using three weeks of unusually high orders. The forecast is precise, but the period may not represent normal conditions.","تتوقع مجموعة لوجستية ارتفاعًا حادًا في الطلب اعتمادًا على ثلاثة أسابيع من الطلبات المرتفعة على نحو غير معتاد. التوقع دقيق رقميًا، لكن الفترة قد لا تمثل الظروف الطبيعية."],["🔬","Ilyas traces the spike to a temporary promotion and asks the team to compare it with seasonal records, stock levels, and ordinary weeks.","يتتبع إلياس الارتفاع إلى عرض ترويجي مؤقت ويطلب مقارنة البيانات بالسجلات الموسمية ومستويات المخزون والأسابيع العادية."],["🧭","The revised model separates promotional demand from baseline demand and shows a range of plausible outcomes. Managers prepare flexible stock plans instead of committing to one brittle number.","يفصل النموذج المعدّل الطلب الناتج عن العرض الترويجي عن الطلب الأساسي ويعرض نطاقًا من النتائج المعقولة. ويعد المديرون خطط مخزون مرنة بدل الالتزام برقم واحد هش."]],"vocab":{"forecast":["a prediction based on available information","توقع","FOR-kast","The forecast uses recent sales."],"baseline":["a starting level used for comparison","مستوى أساسي","BAYS-lyn","Compare results with the baseline."],"plausible":["reasonable and likely to be true","معقول","PLAW-zuh-bul","Several outcomes are plausible."],"brittle":["easily broken or unable to adapt","هش","BRIT-ul","A brittle plan fails when conditions change."]},"questions":[["Why may the original forecast be unreliable?",["The data comes from an unusual promotion period","It contains too many seasonal records","It includes no orders at all"],0,"Three unusually high weeks may not represent ordinary demand."],["What does Ilyas compare the spike with?",["Seasonal records, stock levels, and ordinary weeks","Employee birthdays","The color of delivery trucks"],0,"He asks for several relevant comparisons to understand the spike."],["How does the revised model improve planning?",["It separates baseline and promotional demand and shows a range","It guarantees one exact outcome","It removes all uncertainty"],0,"The model represents different demand drivers and plausible outcomes."]]},
{"id":"c1-cost-convenience","title":"The Cost of Convenience","level":"C1","tone":"#D8B58A","emoji":"🛒","minutes":5,"pages":[["⚙️","A factory considers buying an automated packing line. The supplier emphasizes speed and labor savings, presenting an attractive payback estimate.","يدرس مصنع شراء خط تعبئة آلي. يركز المورد على السرعة وتوفير العمالة ويعرض تقديرًا جذابًا لفترة استرداد التكلفة."],["🧾","The operations analyst includes training, maintenance, downtime, and spare parts. The payback period grows, but the estimate now reflects costs that were previously excluded.","تضيف محللة العمليات تكاليف التدريب والصيانة والتوقف وقطع الغيار. تطول فترة الاسترداد، لكن التقدير يعكس الآن تكاليف كانت مستبعدة."],["🏭","The team runs a pilot on one shift and records both output and interruptions. They postpone a full purchase until the pilot shows whether the convenience creates value under real conditions.","يجري الفريق تجربة على مناوبة واحدة ويسجل الإنتاج والانقطاعات. ويؤجل الشراء الكامل حتى تكشف التجربة إن كانت سهولة التشغيل تحقق قيمة في الظروف الواقعية."]],"vocab":{"payback":["the time needed for an investment to recover its cost","فترة استرداد التكلفة","PAY-bak","The payback period is three years."],"downtime":["time when equipment is not operating","وقت التوقف","DOWN-tym","Maintenance can reduce downtime."],"exclude":["to leave something out","يستبعد","ik-SKLOOD","The first estimate excluded training."],"pilot":["a small test before wider use","تجربة أولية","PY-lut","The factory ran a pilot first."]},"questions":[["What does the supplier emphasize?",["Speed and labor savings","Training failures","Spare-part shortages"],0,"The supplier highlights speed and labor savings."],["Why does the payback period grow?",["The analyst adds previously excluded costs","The line becomes faster","The factory stops recording costs"],0,"Including training, maintenance, downtime, and spare parts raises the estimate."],["Why run a pilot before buying the full line?",["To test value under real operating conditions","To avoid collecting any data","To guarantee zero interruptions"],0,"A pilot checks actual output and interruptions before a large commitment."]]},
{"id":"c1-question-credit","title":"A Question of Credit","level":"C1","tone":"#B8A9DE","emoji":"📝","minutes":5,"pages":[["🏆","A project presentation praises the team lead for an improvement developed largely by a junior engineer, Salma. Salma says nothing during the meeting.","يشيد عرض مشروع بقائد الفريق بسبب تحسين طوّره إلى حد كبير مهندس مبتدئ يُدعى سلمى. لا تقول سلمى شيئًا أثناء الاجتماع."],["🤔","The lead notices her silence and later asks whether the presentation represented the work fairly. Salma explains which tests and design changes she carried out.","يلاحظ القائد صمتها ويسألها لاحقًا إن كان العرض قد مثّل العمل بإنصاف. تشرح سلمى الاختبارات والتغييرات التصميمية التي نفذتها."],["🤝","The lead corrects the project record, credits Salma’s contribution, and agrees to identify responsibilities more clearly in future reviews. The correction improves both recognition and accountability.","يصحح القائد سجل المشروع وينسب مساهمة سلمى إليها ويتفق على تحديد المسؤوليات بوضوح أكبر في المراجعات القادمة. يعزز التصحيح التقدير والمساءلة معًا."]],"vocab":{"contribution":["something a person adds to a shared result","مساهمة","kon-truh-BYOO-shun","Her contribution improved the design."],"represent":["to describe or show something accurately","يمثل","rep-ri-ZENT","The report should represent the work fairly."],"credit":["recognition for someone's work or achievement","تقدير / نسبة الفضل","KRED-it","Give credit to the person who did the work."],"accountability":["responsibility for actions and results","مساءلة","uh-kown-tuh-BIL-uh-tee","Clear roles improve accountability."]},"questions":[["Why does the lead speak to Salma afterward?",["He notices her silence and checks whether the work was represented fairly","He wants her to leave the team","He has lost the presentation"],0,"He asks whether the presentation represented the work fairly."],["What does Salma explain?",["The tests and design changes she carried out","The team's lunch plans","A new office policy"],0,"She describes her own technical contributions."],["What changes after the conversation?",["The record is corrected and responsibilities will be clearer","The project is cancelled","The team stops reviewing work"],0,"The lead corrects the record and agrees on clearer attribution."]]},
{"id":"c1-delayed-warning","title":"The Delayed Warning","level":"C1","tone":"#D8A36F","emoji":"⚡","minutes":5,"pages":[["⚠️","A maintenance dashboard shows a rising vibration trend on a pump. The alert threshold has not been crossed, so the shift team continues operating normally.","تعرض لوحة الصيانة ارتفاعًا تدريجيًا في اهتزاز مضخة. لم يتم تجاوز عتبة الإنذار، لذا يواصل فريق المناوبة التشغيل بشكل طبيعي."],["📉","An engineer compares the trend with previous failures and notices that the current rate of change is unusual. She records the evidence and requests an inspection before the threshold is reached.","يقارن مهندس الاتجاه بأعطال سابقة ويلاحظ أن معدل التغير الحالي غير معتاد. يسجل الأدلة ويطلب فحصًا قبل بلوغ العتبة."],["🛠️","Inspection finds a loose mounting that could have caused damage if left unchecked. The team reviews the alert policy so it considers trend and context, not only a fixed limit.","يكشف الفحص عن تثبيت مرتخٍ كان قد يسبب ضررًا إن تُرك دون معالجة. يراجع الفريق سياسة الإنذار لتراعي الاتجاه والسياق، لا حدًا ثابتًا فقط."]],"vocab":{"threshold":["a level at which an action or change begins","عتبة","THRESH-hold","The alert threshold was not reached."],"trend":["the general direction of change over time","اتجاه","trend","The trend shows rising vibration."],"inspection":["a careful examination","فحص","in-SPEK-shun","The pump needs an inspection."],"context":["the conditions that help explain a fact","سياق","KON-tekst","Context helps explain the measurement."]},"questions":[["Why does the engineer request an inspection early?",["The rate of change is unusual","The pump has already stopped","The threshold is set to zero"],0,"The trend looks unusual compared with previous failures."],["What does the inspection find?",["A loose mounting","An empty fuel tank","A broken display screen"],0,"The inspection identifies a loose mounting."],["What policy change does the team consider?",["Include trend and context in alerts","Remove every alarm","Ignore measurements until a failure"],0,"The team reviews a policy based only on a fixed threshold."]]},
{"id":"c2-metric-mattered","title":"The Metric That Mattered","level":"C2","tone":"#8FBFC4","emoji":"📐","minutes":5,"pages":[["📊","A public service department reports that average waiting time has fallen. Senior leaders celebrate, although complaints about the service have increased.","يعلن قسم خدمة عامة أن متوسط وقت الانتظار انخفض. يحتفل المسؤولون رغم زيادة الشكاوى بشأن الخدمة."],["🔍","An analyst separates routine enquiries from complex cases and finds that the new queue prioritizes short interactions. The average improved partly because the case mix changed, while difficult cases waited longer.","تفصل محللة الاستفسارات الروتينية عن الحالات المعقدة وتكتشف أن الطابور الجديد يعطي الأولوية للتفاعلات القصيرة. تحسن المتوسط جزئيًا بسبب تغير نوع الحالات، بينما انتظرت الحالات الصعبة مدة أطول."],["🧭","The department reports waiting times by case type, alongside completion quality and repeat visits. Leaders revise the target so staff cannot improve the headline metric by neglecting complex users.","يعرض القسم أوقات الانتظار حسب نوع الحالة، إلى جانب جودة الإنجاز والزيارات المتكررة. ويعدل المسؤولون الهدف حتى لا يحسّن الموظفون الرقم الرئيسي على حساب أصحاب الحالات المعقدة."]],"vocab":{"aggregate":["a value formed by combining many individual values","قيمة إجمالية","AG-ri-git","An aggregate average can hide differences."],"case-mix":["the types of cases included in a group of data","تركيبة الحالات","KAYS-miks","A changed case mix affects the average."],"prioritize":["to give something greater importance","يعطي الأولوية","pry-OR-uh-tyze","The queue prioritizes short requests."],"perverse":["having an effect opposite to the intended one","عكسي / غير مرغوب","per-VURS","A poorly designed target can create perverse incentives."]},"questions":[["Why did the average waiting time fall?",["The queue prioritized short interactions and the case mix changed","Every complex case was solved immediately","The department stopped measuring time"],0,"The analyst finds that shorter interactions were prioritized and the mix of cases changed."],["Why are complaints still increasing?",["Complex cases wait longer despite the improved average","There are no complex cases","The average is always meaningless"],0,"The headline average hides longer waits for difficult cases."],["What is the purpose of reporting several measures?",["To reduce the chance of optimizing one metric at users' expense","To make the report longer without reason","To remove accountability"],0,"Case-specific times and quality measures give a more balanced picture."]]},
{"id":"c2-consensus-pressure","title":"A Consensus Under Pressure","level":"C2","tone":"#B5A6D9","emoji":"🏛️","minutes":5,"pages":[["🗳️","A committee must approve a major timetable by the end of the day. The chair asks for objections, but no one speaks. The minutes record unanimous agreement.","يجب على لجنة اعتماد جدول زمني مهم قبل نهاية اليوم. يطلب الرئيس الاعتراضات، لكن لا يتحدث أحد. ويسجل المحضر موافقة بالإجماع."],["🧩","A junior member later tells the facilitator that several people privately doubt the assumptions but fear being seen as obstructive. The silence reflected the room’s hierarchy more than shared confidence.","يخبر عضو مبتدئ الميسّر لاحقًا أن عدة أشخاص يشككون سرًا في الافتراضات لكنهم يخشون الظهور بمظهر المعطّل. عكس الصمت تراتبية الغرفة أكثر مما عكس ثقة مشتركة."],["🗣️","The facilitator reopens the discussion with anonymous risk statements and asks the committee to distinguish unresolved concerns from acceptable trade-offs. The final decision is slower but better informed.","يعيد الميسّر فتح النقاش عبر إفادات مجهولة عن المخاطر ويطلب من اللجنة التمييز بين المخاوف غير المحسومة والمفاضلات المقبولة. يصبح القرار النهائي أبطأ لكنه أكثر استنارة."]],"vocab":{"unanimous":["in agreement by everyone","بالإجماع","yoo-NAN-uh-mus","The minutes recorded unanimous agreement."],"hierarchy":["a system of ranks or levels of authority","تراتبية","HY-uh-rar-kee","Hierarchy can affect who speaks."],"obstructive":["making progress difficult on purpose or in effect","معطّل","ub-STRUK-tiv","They feared being called obstructive."],"trade-off":["a situation where one benefit requires giving up another","مفاضلة","TRAYD-off","The committee discussed the trade-off."]},"questions":[["What does the silence initially appear to mean?",["Unanimous agreement","A cancelled meeting","A technical failure"],0,"The minutes record unanimous agreement because no one objects."],["What does the junior member reveal?",["Some members doubt assumptions but fear speaking","Everyone fully supports the timetable","The committee has no deadline"],0,"Several people privately doubt the assumptions and fear appearing obstructive."],["Why use anonymous risk statements?",["To surface concerns that hierarchy may suppress","To remove the need for evidence","To guarantee everyone agrees"],0,"Anonymous statements can make it safer to raise concerns under social pressure."]]},
{"id":"c2-ambiguous-promise","title":"The Ambiguous Promise","level":"C2","tone":"#D6AA83","emoji":"🗣️","minutes":5,"pages":[["📄","A director tells a partner, “We should be able to deliver the revised system by June.” The partner records June as a firm commitment and schedules a public launch.","يقول مدير لشريك: «ينبغي أن نتمكن من تسليم النظام المعدّل بحلول يونيو». يسجل الشريك يونيو باعتباره التزامًا مؤكدًا ويحدد موعد إطلاق عام."],["🔎","When the team later explains that testing could extend the timeline, both sides feel misled. The director intended a conditional forecast; the partner heard a promise.","عندما يوضح الفريق لاحقًا أن الاختبارات قد تمدد الجدول، يشعر الطرفان بأنهما تعرضا للتضليل. قصد المدير توقعًا مشروطًا، بينما فهم الشريك وعدًا."],["🤝","They revisit the wording and separate the target date from the decision criteria: June remains the goal if reliability tests pass by a stated checkpoint. Each side confirms the same interpretation in writing.","يعيدان صياغة العبارة ويفصلان التاريخ المستهدف عن معايير القرار: يظل يونيو هدفًا إذا اجتازت اختبارات الاعتمادية نقطة تحقق محددة. ويؤكد كل طرف الفهم نفسه كتابةً."]],"vocab":{"conditional":["depending on something else being true","مشروط","kun-DISH-uh-nul","The date is conditional on test results."],"commitment":["a promise or firm obligation","التزام","kuh-MIT-ment","The partner understood it as a commitment."],"interpretation":["the meaning someone understands from a statement","تفسير","in-tur-pruh-TAY-shun","Their interpretations were different."],"checkpoint":["a planned moment to review progress or evidence","نقطة تحقق","CHECK-point","The team set a checkpoint in May."]},"questions":[["Why do the two sides disagree about June?",["They interpret a conditional forecast differently","The system has already launched","The partner changes the month"],0,"The director intends a conditional forecast while the partner hears a firm promise."],["What risk does the misunderstanding create?",["The partner schedules a public launch too early","The team stops testing completely","The deadline disappears from the calendar"],0,"The partner treats June as guaranteed and schedules a launch."],["How do they reduce future ambiguity?",["Separate the target from conditions and confirm it in writing","Avoid discussing dates ever again","Let each side keep its own interpretation"],0,"They define a goal, a test condition, and a checkpoint, then confirm the shared meaning."]]},
{"id":"c2-missing-counterfactual","title":"The Missing Counterfactual","level":"C2","tone":"#9DB8E0","emoji":"🧠","minutes":5,"pages":[["📈","A city introduces a new traffic signal pattern. Travel time falls by eight percent in the following month, and the report attributes the entire improvement to the change.","تطبق مدينة نمطًا جديدًا لإشارات المرور. ينخفض زمن الرحلة بنسبة ثمانية بالمئة في الشهر التالي، وينسب التقرير التحسن كله إلى التغيير."],["🔬","An evaluator notes that roadworks also ended during that month and school holidays altered traffic. Without a comparison, the observed change cannot isolate the signal pattern’s effect.","يلاحظ مقيّم أن أعمال الطرق انتهت أيضًا خلال ذلك الشهر وأن العطلات المدرسية غيّرت حركة المرور. من دون مقارنة، لا يمكن عزل أثر نمط الإشارات عن بقية العوامل."],["🧭","The city compares similar corridors and historical periods, while acknowledging remaining limitations. The signal pattern appears to help, but the report narrows its claim and recommends continued monitoring.","تقارن المدينة ممرات مرورية مشابهة وفترات تاريخية مع الإقرار بالقيود المتبقية. يبدو أن نمط الإشارات مفيد، لكن التقرير يضيّق ادعاءه ويوصي بمواصلة المراقبة."]],"vocab":{"attribute":["to say that something was caused by a person or thing","ينسب","uh-TRIB-yoot","The report attributes the change to the new plan."],"counterfactual":["a comparison with what might have happened otherwise","حالة افتراضية مضادة","kown-ter-FAK-choo-ul","A counterfactual helps assess what would happen without the intervention."],"isolate":["to identify one factor separately from others","يعزل","EYE-suh-layt","The comparison tries to isolate the effect."],"limitation":["a condition that restricts what can be concluded","قيد","lim-ih-TAY-shun","The report explains its limitations."]},"questions":[["Why is the original causal claim weak?",["Other changes happened at the same time","Travel time increased in every period","The signal pattern was never changed"],0,"Roadworks ended and school holidays altered traffic during the same month."],["What does a comparison help the evaluator do?",["Separate the signal effect from other factors","Prove every result with certainty","Ignore historical information"],0,"Comparable corridors and periods help assess the intervention more carefully."],["How does the final report change?",["It narrows the claim and recommends monitoring","It claims absolute proof","It removes all mention of limitations"],0,"The report acknowledges limits while saying the signal pattern appears to help."]]}];

const STORY_DECISIONS = {"a1-lost-key":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"What should Mia do next?","options":[{"text":"Ask someone for help.","response":"Asking for help can be useful when you are stuck."},{"text":"Look carefully in one more place.","response":"Good thinking: checking carefully may solve the problem."},{"text":"Give up and leave.","response":"Sometimes a short pause helps, but giving up too early can miss a solution."}]},"a1-rainy-picnic":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"The rain starts. What is the best plan?","options":[{"text":"Find a dry place and keep the picnic.","response":"A flexible plan lets Sam and his sister enjoy the day."},{"text":"Leave the food in the rain.","response":"Food can get wet, so protecting it is a practical first step."},{"text":"Wait outside until the rain stops.","response":"Waiting is possible, but a nearby shelter may be more comfortable."}]},"a2-night-train":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"How can Nora help the man?","options":[{"text":"Ask where he last saw the suitcase.","response":"A clear question helps narrow down where to look."},{"text":"Tell him to buy another suitcase.","response":"Replacing something is costly; checking the facts first is wiser."},{"text":"Ignore him because the train is late.","response":"A small act of help can make a difficult wait easier."}]},"a2-bread-mystery":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"Leo wants to find out what happened. What should he do?","options":[{"text":"Watch quietly before blaming anyone.","response":"Observing first helps Leo avoid accusing the wrong person."},{"text":"Accuse his brother again.","response":"Blaming someone without evidence can hurt trust."},{"text":"Hide all the food forever.","response":"Protecting the bread may help, but it will not explain the mystery."}]},"b1-last-bus":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"Would you take the cyclist’s advice?","options":[{"text":"Check the route and try it.","response":"Checking a suggestion, then acting quickly, balances caution and initiative."},{"text":"Call a taxi without listening.","response":"A taxi is an option, but it may cost more than necessary."},{"text":"Stay at the same stop.","response":"Waiting may not help if the last bus has already left."}]},"b1-quiet-lab":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"What should the team test first?","options":[{"text":"Close the window and repeat the measurement.","response":"Changing one variable at a time is a useful way to test a cause."},{"text":"Replace every sensor immediately.","response":"Replacing equipment before testing can waste time and money."},{"text":"Ignore the strange readings.","response":"Unexpected results are clues worth investigating."}]},"b2-open-door":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"How should the manager respond to blunt feedback?","options":[{"text":"Listen and look for a pattern.","response":"Listening for recurring concerns can reveal the real bottleneck."},{"text":"Defend every decision immediately.","response":"Defensiveness can discourage people from speaking honestly."},{"text":"Cancel all future meetings.","response":"The problem is not necessarily meetings, but how decisions are made."}]},"b2-second-chance":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"What would help Rafi improve?","options":[{"text":"Review the recording and practise in small steps.","response":"Specific feedback and steady practice make improvement manageable."},{"text":"Avoid speaking in public again.","response":"Avoidance may reduce anxiety briefly but limits practice."},{"text":"Pretend the speech went perfectly.","response":"Honest reflection gives Rafi something useful to improve."}]},"c1-quiet-objection":{"afterPage":1,"prompt":"The team is uncomfortable with Leila’s question. What should she do next?","options":[{"text":"Ask for the evidence behind the estimates and invite the team to review it together.","response":"This keeps the discussion focused on evidence, gives colleagues a shared problem to solve, and avoids turning the question into a personal confrontation."},{"text":"Withdraw the concern so the meeting can finish on time.","response":"This may preserve short-term comfort, but the uncertainty remains hidden and the team loses a chance to reduce the risk."},{"text":"Insist that the schedule is wrong before checking the records.","response":"Raising a risk matters, but declaring the plan wrong before checking evidence can weaken trust and make a useful concern easier to dismiss."}]},"c1-cost-of-clarity":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A report claims a process is faster but leaves out maintenance. What do you ask?","options":[{"text":"What costs or trade-offs are missing?","response":"Asking about trade-offs makes the comparison more useful."},{"text":"Can we remove the limitations section?","response":"Removing limitations makes a report less reliable."},{"text":"Is the report longer than before?","response":"Length alone does not tell us whether the evidence is complete."}]},"c2-language-of-consensus":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A committee seems unanimous, but several people are silent. What should the chair do?","options":[{"text":"Invite objections before confirming the decision.","response":"Inviting dissent helps distinguish genuine consensus from acquiescence."},{"text":"Treat silence as full agreement.","response":"Silence may reflect pressure rather than genuine agreement."},{"text":"End the meeting immediately.","response":"A short invitation to disagree may uncover important risks."}]},"c2-unintended-inference":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A colleague calls your plan “ambitious.” How do you clarify the meaning?","options":[{"text":"Ask which milestones need stronger evidence.","response":"A specific question turns an ambiguous comment into actionable feedback."},{"text":"Assume they are insulting the plan.","response":"The word can signal praise or doubt; context matters."},{"text":"Ignore the comment entirely.","response":"Clarifying the concern can prevent misunderstandings later."}]},
"a1-blue-umbrella":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The man is getting wet. What can Ana do?","options":[{"text":"Share her umbrella.","response":"Sharing gives both people some protection from the rain."},{"text":"Laugh and walk away.","response":"That would leave someone who needs help in the rain."},{"text":"Hide her umbrella.","response":"Keeping it to herself would not help the man."}]},
"a1-helpful-neighbor":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"Ben's bucket is broken. What should he do?","options":[{"text":"Ask a neighbor for help.","response":"Asking politely can help solve a simple problem."},{"text":"Leave the flowers without water forever.","response":"The flowers still need water, so the problem remains."},{"text":"Throw away all the flowers.","response":"That is not necessary when the problem is the bucket."}]},
"a1-wrong-lunchbox":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The food in the box is not Lina's. What should she do?","options":[{"text":"Check the name on the box.","response":"Checking the name helps her find the right owner."},{"text":"Eat everything quickly.","response":"The food may belong to another student."},{"text":"Hide the lunchbox.","response":"Hiding it will not help either student find their food."}]},
"a1-note-grandma":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"Tom has written a note. What should he do next?","options":[{"text":"Take it to Grandma.","response":"Taking the note to her lets her read his message."},{"text":"Throw it into the river.","response":"Then Grandma will not receive the message."},{"text":"Forget the visit.","response":"He wants to see Grandma, so he can continue with his plan."}]},
"a2-library-card":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"Nora has never used the library. What is a good first step?","options":[{"text":"Ask the librarian how to register.","response":"The librarian can explain the process and required information."},{"text":"Take a book without telling anyone.","response":"Books must be checked out so the library can track them."},{"text":"Leave without asking a question.","response":"She would miss the help that makes borrowing straightforward."}]},
"a2-room-for-two":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The room does not match their needs. What should Maya do?","options":[{"text":"Explain the problem politely.","response":"A clear, respectful explanation helps the clerk find a solution."},{"text":"Shout before checking the booking.","response":"Anger may make the conversation harder without adding useful information."},{"text":"Say nothing and accept it.","response":"The mismatch may be fixable if the hotel knows about it."}]},
"a2-early-delivery":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"Karim is at work when the driver calls. What should he do?","options":[{"text":"Arrange a safe handover with a trusted person.","response":"A confirmed handover gives the driver a clear and safer option."},{"text":"Tell the driver to leave it anywhere.","response":"An unattended package could be lost or taken."},{"text":"Share his account password.","response":"A delivery does not require sharing a private password."}]},
"a2-garden-map":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The sign seems confusing. What should they do?","options":[{"text":"Compare the sign with the map.","response":"Using two sources helps them make a more informed choice."},{"text":"Run in a random direction.","response":"Moving without checking may take them farther from the group."},{"text":"Throw the map away.","response":"The map is useful information they should keep."}]},
"b1-unsent-message":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"Daniel is angry but is not sure what happened. What is the best next step?","options":[{"text":"Pause and check the facts first.","response":"A short pause can prevent an accusation based on an untested assumption."},{"text":"Send the harshest version immediately.","response":"An immediate accusation may damage trust before the facts are clear."},{"text":"Tell the whole team the colleague is careless.","response":"Public blame spreads an unverified conclusion instead of solving the communication problem."}]},
"b1-small-repair":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The chain slips off while Amina is late. What matters most first?","options":[{"text":"Move somewhere safe and inspect the problem.","response":"Safety comes before speed, and inspection helps avoid further damage."},{"text":"Pedal harder until it works.","response":"Forcing the pedals could damage the bicycle or cause a fall."},{"text":"Ride into traffic to save time.","response":"That increases risk instead of solving the mechanical problem."}]},
"b1-shared-budget":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The group has different ideas and little money. What should they do first?","options":[{"text":"Agree on the requirements and compare options.","response":"Shared requirements make comparisons fairer and keep the group focused."},{"text":"Let the loudest person decide everything.","response":"That may ignore important needs and useful alternatives."},{"text":"Buy materials before checking prices.","response":"Buying first risks spending the limited budget too quickly."}]},
"b1-missing-minutes":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The chat contains two possible dates. What should Yusuf do?","options":[{"text":"Ask the group to confirm the final decision.","response":"Confirmation prevents a guess from becoming an incorrect record."},{"text":"Choose the date he likes best.","response":"Personal preference does not establish what the group agreed."},{"text":"Delete both dates without asking.","response":"Removing information would leave the uncertainty unresolved."}]},
"b2-honest-estimate":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The manager wants one date, but key tasks remain uncertain. How should Noor respond?","options":[{"text":"Explain a realistic range and what evidence would narrow it.","response":"A transparent range supports planning while making uncertainty and next steps explicit."},{"text":"Promise the earliest date to sound confident.","response":"An unsupported promise can create avoidable pressure and damage trust."},{"text":"Refuse to estimate anything.","response":"A useful range is possible even when the exact duration is unknown."}]},
"b2-better-handoff":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The same information is missing from many handoffs. What is the best response?","options":[{"text":"Find the recurring gaps and design a simple template.","response":"A shared structure addresses the repeated cause while keeping the process practical."},{"text":"Blame each person separately without changing the process.","response":"Individual reminders may not fix a recurring system-level gap."},{"text":"Require a long report for every small case.","response":"Excessive documentation can add friction without guaranteeing useful information."}]},
"b2-quiet-customer":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A regular customer stops visiting, but the reason is unknown. What should the team do?","options":[{"text":"Ask respectfully and listen before deciding.","response":"Direct feedback tests the assumption and may reveal a fixable experience problem."},{"text":"Assume price is the only cause.","response":"An untested assumption may lead to the wrong solution."},{"text":"Ignore the change because other reviews are positive.","response":"Positive feedback does not explain why this particular customer left."}]},
"b2-data-gap":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"The data looks positive, but the periods are not comparable. What should the team do?","options":[{"text":"Correct the comparison before making a claim.","response":"Comparable periods help separate a real effect from a measurement difference."},{"text":"Publish the strongest number immediately.","response":"That risks overstating the evidence and weakening trust."},{"text":"Discard all the data without review.","response":"The data may still be useful once the comparison is made fairly."}]},
"c1-fragile-forecast":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A precise forecast relies on a short, unusual period. What is the strongest response?","options":[{"text":"Test whether the period represents normal conditions.","response":"Precision is not the same as reliability; representative data matters."},{"text":"Treat the number as certain because it has decimals.","response":"Extra decimal places cannot correct biased or unrepresentative data."},{"text":"Ignore every recent order.","response":"Recent data is useful, but it needs context rather than automatic rejection."}]},
"c1-cost-convenience":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A proposal looks attractive but excludes recurring costs. What should the team do?","options":[{"text":"Include the full lifecycle costs and test key assumptions.","response":"A complete cost model and a pilot give a more credible basis for investment."},{"text":"Approve it because the initial estimate is simple.","response":"Simplicity does not compensate for missing costs that may change the decision."},{"text":"Reject automation without examining the evidence.","response":"The omitted costs matter, but the technology may still be worthwhile after a fair assessment."}]},
"c1-question-credit":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A presentation may have overlooked a colleague's contribution. What is a constructive response?","options":[{"text":"Check the record and correct attribution with specific evidence.","response":"Specific evidence allows recognition to be corrected without relying on vague accusation."},{"text":"Assume the omission was deliberate and accuse the lead publicly.","response":"Intent is not yet established; a factual conversation is more likely to repair the record."},{"text":"Ignore it because the project succeeded.","response":"A successful outcome does not remove the need for fair recognition and accountability."}]},
"c1-delayed-warning":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A warning threshold has not been crossed, but the trend looks unusual. What should the engineer do?","options":[{"text":"Document the trend and assess the risk in context.","response":"A trend can reveal emerging risk before a fixed threshold is crossed."},{"text":"Ignore it because the alarm is still quiet.","response":"A threshold is useful, but it may not capture every developing failure."},{"text":"Declare that failure is certain.","response":"An unusual trend justifies investigation, not an unsupported certainty."}]},
"c2-metric-mattered":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A headline metric improves while complaints rise. What should the analyst investigate?","options":[{"text":"Check subgroup results and whether incentives changed behavior.","response":"Disaggregated data can expose trade-offs hidden by an aggregate metric and reveal unintended incentives."},{"text":"Declare the service successful based on the average alone.","response":"A single aggregate measure cannot explain the rise in complaints."},{"text":"Stop collecting complaint data.","response":"Removing a conflicting signal conceals the problem rather than resolving it."}]},
"c2-consensus-pressure":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A committee is silent under time pressure. Can silence safely be treated as consensus?","options":[{"text":"Invite concerns through a safer, structured process.","response":"Structured dissent helps distinguish genuine agreement from silence caused by status or fear."},{"text":"Record agreement immediately because no one objected.","response":"Silence is ambiguous, especially when hierarchy or deadlines make dissent costly."},{"text":"Assume every member secretly opposes the plan.","response":"That overcorrects in the other direction; concerns should be elicited rather than presumed."}]},
"c2-ambiguous-promise":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"A partner treats a qualified forecast as a firm promise. What should the director clarify?","options":[{"text":"State the target, conditions, and checkpoint explicitly.","response":"Separating an aspiration from its conditions makes expectations testable and reduces interpretive risk."},{"text":"Insist the partner should have guessed the intended meaning.","response":"When wording permits two plausible readings, relying on inference leaves the mismatch unresolved."},{"text":"Remove all dates from future discussions.","response":"Avoiding dates sacrifices useful planning rather than making commitments clearer."}]},
"c2-missing-counterfactual":{"afterPage":0,"prompt":"An outcome improves after a policy change, but other factors changed too. What conclusion is justified?","options":[{"text":"Compare plausible alternatives and qualify the causal claim.","response":"A counterfactual comparison helps estimate the intervention’s contribution without overstating certainty."},{"text":"Attribute the entire improvement to the policy.","response":"Timing alone does not establish causation when other changes coincide."},{"text":"Conclude the policy had no effect at all.","response":"Confounding factors limit certainty; they do not automatically prove the intervention had no effect."}]}
}
for (const story of STORIES) { if (STORY_DECISIONS[story.id]) story.decision = STORY_DECISIONS[story.id]; }
for (const s of STORIES) { s.pages=s.pages.map(([scene,text,ar])=>({scene,text,ar})); s.questions=s.questions.map(([q,answers,correct,explain])=>({q,sub:'Choose the best answer.',answers,correct,explain})); const vocab={}; for(const [k,v] of Object.entries(s.vocab))vocab[k]={meaning:v[0],ar:v[1],pronunciation:v[2],example:v[3]};s.vocab=vocab; }